      "id": "i4lvch7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FRAMING OF THE INDIAN CONSTITUTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "M.N. Roy first put forward the idea of a Constituent Assembly for India in 1934.",
        "The Constituent Assembly was constituted in November 1946 under the scheme formulated by the Cabinet Mission Plan.",
        "Dr. Sachchidananda Sinha was appointed as the temporary President for the first meeting on December 9, 1946.",
        "Jawaharlal Nehru moved the historic 'Objectives Resolution' on December 13, 1946, which formed the basis of the Preamble.",
        "Dr. B.R. Ambedkar served as the Chairman of the Drafting Committee, which comprised seven members."
      ],
      "id": "jxwvu95"
    },
